    "created_at": "2025-06-11T18:39:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-06-11T18:39:03Z",
    "body": "This behavior is intended to work around a platform limitation on Windows. On Windows, Chrome can't reliably get the report descriptor and instead uses higher-level HID APIs to determine report layout. Also, Windows HID APIs expect applications to size all report buffers according to the maximum report of that type (input, output, feature). To satisfy this, Chrome inserts a padding item to pad the report to that length. If you compute the buffer size by summing reportCount*reportSize for each item in the report then you'll get the \"correct\" buffer size (maximum report length on Windows, true report length on other platforms).",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
