    "updated_at": "2025-06-12T00:05:12Z",
    "body": "[HIDDevice.collections](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#dom-hiddevice-collections) contains the information that would normally be in the HID report descriptor.\n\nA HIDDevice's reports are grouped into [HIDCollectionInfos](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#hidcollectioninfo-dictionary). The collection's input reports are listed in HIDCollectionInfo.inputReports. Each [HIDReportInfo](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#hidreportinfo-dictionary) in the reports list has a `reportId` (the report's ID, or 0 if the device doesn't use numbered reports) and an `items` list containing [HIDReportItems](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#hidreportitem-dictionary).\n\nEach item represents a field within the report. The items have the same ordering as the report fields and there are no gaps between items, so the total size of all items in HIDReportInfo.items is equal to the total size of the report.\n\nTo compute the total report length (in bits), iterate over the `items` list summing [reportSize](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#dom-hidreportitem-reportsize) \\* [reportCount](https://wicg.github.io/webhid/#dom-hidreportitem-reportcount).",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
